Z||000000||Philphine||08-04-2000||09:48 AM||||<BR>i'm struggling with keeping my indy somewhat original. i will make changes but i'm meaning to be able to go back to original if i want.<P>one thing is the stereo. i was bidding on some door panels on ebay but let them go once they got beyond $100. what is an acceptable price for indy door panels. or, since i would be using the extra panels to work in some speakers and would have to do some refinishing any way, has anyone bought regular panels and refinished them to look like indys? i've used vinyl paint before but don't know where to find that shade of gray (a little lighter than normal panels. the carpet part hopefully i can find. <P>thanks for any help.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||LAMBO||08-04-2000||10:14 AM||||Check with Mr. Mike's. I think you can get correct carpet panels for the doors from him. The lighter shade of gray is a hard match if your trying to do it yourself, but it can be done. I don't think that it is a color that was only in the Indys though. I'd swear my 85 SE has that same light shade of gray in it. Haven't checked them side by side to know for sure. Also, you can get refurbished leather wrapped armrests/handles from Mr. Mike's too. Check with Fiero Dave. I bought my Indy from him. He did an excellent resto on it and he could probably steer you in all the right directions. Hope I helped. Lambo||||reg||1
Z||000002||007DOUG||08-04-2000||12:00 PM||||The indy uses the 84 light grey panels.<P>Buy a set of 84 panels, and dye the carpet part red.<P>I too was bidding on the panels, and stopped. They were non-power panels. Not stated in the description, but shown in the picture.<P>------------------<BR><I>"Time is simultaneously my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||NDFieroTN||08-04-2000||11:45 PM||||Philphine...Give FieroDave a call...he can be ALOT of help and can refinish a set of armrests, steering wheel, and shifter knob for you...He did them on both of my Indys and they look great...||||reg||6
